### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 12 — MCP SERVER + CLIENT TESTING
###
### Tool: REST Client (humao.rest-client) for VS Code
###
### How session ID flows between requests:
###   1. Run [MCP-1] — it is named with # @name mcpInit
###   2. The variable @mcpSessionId is set from that response header
###   3. All subsequent requests use {{mcpSessionId}} in the header
###
### IMPORTANT: Run requests in order — MCP-1 must be sent before
###            any request that uses {{mcpSessionId}}.
###
### ArcClaw exposes two MCP surfaces:
###
###   A) MCP SERVER (inbound) — Quarkiverse endpoint at /mcp
###      Handshake: initialize → notifications/initialized → tools/list → tools/call
###
###   B) MCP CLIENT (outbound) — McpConnectResource
###      POST   /api/v1/mcp/connect        → connect to remote server
###      DELETE /api/v1/mcp/connect/{name} → disconnect + deregister tools
###      GET    /api/v1/mcp/connect        → list connected servers
###
###   C) MCP ADMIN (read-only)
###      GET /api/v1/mcp/status  → enabled flag + dynamic tool count
###      GET /api/v1/mcp/tools   → exposed internal + dynamic tools
###
### Telegram: /mcp → McpReflex shows live MCP status
###
### Prerequisites:
###   ArcClaw running in serve mode
###   arcclaw.mcp.server-enabled=true (default)
###   McpConnectResource.java added to arcclaw-app/.../mcp/
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@adminBase = http://localhost:8080/api/v1
@mcpBase   = http://localhost:8080
@validKey  = key-internal-cWevfEoRvstUv0PqGpf02LzDY5kPNaz1y9GSl0LZOwU=


### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### FLOW A — MCP ADMIN (run first as health checks)
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### [MCP-ADMIN-1] Check MCP server status
# Expect 200: {"serverEnabled":true,"dynamicToolCount":0}
# If 404 → arcclaw.mcp.server-enabled=false in config
GET {{adminBase}}/mcp/status
Accept: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [MCP-ADMIN-2] List all MCP tools — internal exposed + dynamic registered
# Expect 200:
# {
#   "exposedInternalTools": [{"name":"github",...},{"name":"memory_search",...}],
#   "registeredDynamicTools": []   ← empty until FLOW D runs
# }
GET {{adminBase}}/mcp/tools
Accept: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###


### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### FLOW B — MCP PROTOCOL (ArcClaw as server, you as client)
###
### Run in strict order: MCP-1 → MCP-2 → MCP-3 → MCP-4 → MCP-5
###
### After sending MCP-1, the @mcpSessionId variable below is
### populated automatically from the response header. Every
### request from MCP-2 onwards sends it as Mcp-Session-Id.
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### [MCP-1] Initialize — start the MCP handshake
# Expect 200: JSON-RPC result with protocolVersion + capabilities
# Mcp-Session-Id is captured from the response header below.
# @name mcpInit
POST {{mcpBase}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 1,
  "method": "initialize",
  "params": {
    "protocolVersion": "2024-11-05",
    "capabilities": {},
    "clientInfo": {
      "name": "rest-client-test",
      "version": "1.0"
    }
  }
}

###

# Capture session ID from MCP-1 response header — must appear after MCP-1
@mcpSessionId = {{mcpInit.response.headers.mcp-session-id}}

###

### [MCP-2] Send notifications/initialized — completes the handshake
# Expect 202: empty body (notification, no JSON-RPC response per spec)
# MUST be sent before tools/list or tools/call
POST {{mcpBase}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}
Mcp-Session-Id: {{mcpSessionId}}

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "method": "notifications/initialized",
  "params": {}
}

###

### [MCP-3] List tools — discover what ArcClaw exposes
# Expect 200: tools array containing "github" and "memory_search"
# These come from arcclaw.mcp.exposed-tools via McpToolBridge
POST {{mcpBase}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}
Mcp-Session-Id: {{mcpSessionId}}

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 2,
  "method": "tools/list",
  "params": {}
}

###

### [MCP-4] Call memory_search tool
# Expect 200: result.content[0].text = memory search output
# Flow: McpToolsBean.memorySearch() → McpToolBridge.invoke()
#       → ToolRegistry.invokeTool() → memory search impl
# Audit event MCP_TOOL_INVOKED persisted for every call
POST {{mcpBase}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}
Mcp-Session-Id: {{mcpSessionId}}

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 3,
  "method": "tools/call",
  "params": {
    "name": "memory_search",
    "arguments": {
      "query": "ArcClaw architecture overview"
    }
  }
}

###

### [MCP-5] Call github tool
# Expect 200: result.content[0].text = github output
# Returns an error string inside content if GH_TOKEN not seeded — still HTTP 200
POST {{mcpBase}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}
Mcp-Session-Id: {{mcpSessionId}}

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 4,
  "method": "tools/call",
  "params": {
    "name": "github",
    "arguments": {
      "operation": "list_repos",
      "paramsJson": "{}"
    }
  }
}

###


### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### FLOW C — MCP ERROR / EDGE CASES
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### [MCP-ERR-1] Call a tool NOT in the allowlist
# Expect 200 HTTP with JSON-RPC error body (per JSON-RPC spec errors are HTTP 200)
# {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":5,"error":{"code":...,"message":"Tool 'sandbox_exec' not in allowlist"}}
POST {{mcpBase}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}
Mcp-Session-Id: {{mcpSessionId}}

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 5,
  "method": "tools/call",
  "params": {
    "name": "sandbox_exec",
    "arguments": {}
  }
}

###

### [MCP-ERR-2] tools/list without session ID → expect 4xx
# Quarkiverse MCP session validation rejects missing Mcp-Session-Id header
POST {{mcpBase}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 6,
  "method": "tools/list",
  "params": {}
}

###


### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### FLOW D — MCP CLIENT (ArcClaw connecting OUT to remote servers)
###
### Prerequisite: McpConnectResource.java added at:
###   arcclaw-app/src/main/java/com/arcclaw/app/mcp/McpConnectResource.java
###
### Self-connect smoke test — no external server needed:
###   MCP-CLIENT-1 connects ArcClaw to itself (localhost:8080/mcp).
###   After MCP-CLIENT-1 succeeds:
###     MCP-ADMIN-2 → registeredDynamicTools has 2 entries
###     /mcp in Telegram → "Dynamic MCP tools (2): github [self, HTTP_SSE]..."
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### [MCP-CLIENT-1] Self-connect — ArcClaw connects to itself as an MCP client
# Expect 200: {"name":"self","url":"...","toolsRegistered":2,"status":"connected"}
# Proves the full outbound client stack:
#   McpConnectResource → McpClientService.connect() →
#   MCP initialize handshake → tools/list → DynamicToolCapabilityRegistry.register()
POST {{adminBase}}/mcp/connect
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
  "name": "self",
  "url": "http://localhost:8080/mcp"
}

###

### [MCP-CLIENT-2] Verify dynamic tools are now registered
# Expect 200: registeredDynamicTools contains github + memory_search
# both with mcpServerName="self" and transport="HTTP_SSE"
GET {{adminBase}}/mcp/tools
Accept: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [MCP-CLIENT-3] List connected servers
# Expect 200: {"connectedServers":[{"name":"self","url":"(url not stored)","toolCount":2}],"totalDynamicTools":2}
GET {{adminBase}}/mcp/connect
Accept: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [MCP-CLIENT-4] Connect to a real external MCP server (edit url and uncomment)
# After connecting, the agent can invoke those tools naturally via Telegram.
# POST {{adminBase}}/mcp/connect
# Content-Type: application/json
# X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}
#
# {
#   "name": "remote",
#   "url": "http://your-mcp-server:3000/mcp"
# }

###

### [MCP-CLIENT-5] Disconnect the self server
# Expect 200: {"name":"self","deregistered":true,"toolsRemoved":2}
# After this:
#   MCP-ADMIN-2 shows registeredDynamicTools: []
#   /mcp in Telegram → "Dynamic MCP tools: none connected"
DELETE {{adminBase}}/mcp/connect/self
Accept: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [MCP-CLIENT-6] Verify dynamic tools cleared after disconnect
# Expect 200: registeredDynamicTools: []
GET {{adminBase}}/mcp/tools
Accept: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###


### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### FLOW E — MCP CLIENT ERROR / EDGE CASES
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### [MCP-CLIENT-ERR-1] Connect with missing url → expect 400
POST {{adminBase}}/mcp/connect
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
  "name": "no-url"
}

###

### [MCP-CLIENT-ERR-2] Connect to unreachable server → expect 502
# McpClientService throws McpConnectionException → McpConnectResource returns 502
POST {{adminBase}}/mcp/connect
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
  "name": "dead",
  "url": "http://localhost:9999/mcp"
}

###

### [MCP-CLIENT-ERR-3] Disconnect a server never connected → expect 404
DELETE {{adminBase}}/mcp/connect/never-connected
Accept: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [MCP-CLIENT-ERR-4] Connect without API key → expect 401
POST {{adminBase}}/mcp/connect
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "unauth",
  "url": "http://localhost:8080/mcp"
}

###
